From 754aa8048b6b067154c26491248b37e4f33802b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 01:37:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Select LLVM options for assembler and compiler actions

Keep preprocessor definitions and include paths on preprocessing actions, and source compiler, random-seed, and code-generation options on compiler actions. Preserve assembler target selection and fatal warning enforcement. Cover raw assembly, preprocessed assembly, and C in fastbuild, debug, and optimized modes through the maintained warning check.

The raw assembly probe reproduces unused-command-line-argument errors with LLVM 0.8.24. Optimized mode additionally reproduces invalid optimization and macro flags. just check-build-warnings for windows_x86_64_gnullvm passes all three modes and the expected negative warning check after the repair. Native Linux and fresh emitted-patch checks follow in the owning verification record.
